'''Chroma Gingerblade''' is a [[Chroma Weapons|chroma]] knife that was originally obtainable by unboxing it from the [[2018 Christmas box|Christmas Box]] during the [[Christmas Event 2018|2018 Christmas Event]]. It is now only obtainable through trading as the event has since ended.  

== Appearance ==
Chroma Gingerblade is a knife that is primarily made of gingerbread, hence the name. On the blade, it has white icing and small bits of candy. The guard consists of a rather large peppermint with pieces of gingerbread, along with icing attached to it. Contrasting from the rest of the knife, the handle is made out of only candy covered in icing. All of the candy on this knife alternates in color. 

== Trivia ==
*It is the chroma counterpart of the [[Godly Weapons|godly]] knife under the name [[Gingerblade]], which was found in the same box. 
*Chroma Gingerblade was the first Christmas chroma and the second ever holiday chroma to be released inside the game, the first being [[Chroma Boneblade]].
*This and all the other holiday chromas are the only [[Chroma Weapons]] that are no longer unboxable.
*Chroma Gingerblade was in the first [[Christmas Event 2018|Christmas]] [[Boxes|box]] to feature both [[knives]] and [[guns]] in the box.
*It lost a lot of value after [[The Duping Glitch (2019)|The Duping Glitch (2019).]]
*Like all the other [[Chroma Weapons]], it is not salvageable in the crafting station.
*There currently is a glitch where, if a player throws this knife, the Chroma part of the weapon will not be thrown and will stay on the player's hand, while the Non-Chroma part of the weapon will be thrown. This glitch currently remains unfixed.
*A glitch occurs when the [[Ghostify]] effect is used on this knife, causing the knife to be surrounded by a white translucent rectangle. The rectangle represents the size of the knife’s hitbox. This glitch also affects the non-chroma [[Gingerblade]].
*Using the "/chromatoggle" command on Chroma Gingerblade will cause the entire knife to turn rainbow instead of the selected candy parts.[[File:Cgingerbladectogglebug.png|thumb|Chroma Gingerblade after using the "/chromatoggle" command.]]

